{'user_input': 'What is the operator procedure to put a private deployment tenant into local-only telemetry mode and how can you verify the mode afterward?', 'response': "Based on the provided context, the operator procedure to put a tenant into local-only telemetry mode is:\n\n1. In the control plane: open tenant config → Telemetry → select 'no-external-telemetry' → apply\n2. CLI fallback: `redwoodctl tenant update --id <ID> --telemetry-mode local-only`\n\nTo verify the mode afterward, validate with:\n`curl -sS http://localhost:9100/telemetry/status?tenant=<TENANT_ID>`\n\n(Note: the context text is partially truncated/garbled in the provided chunks, so the exact CLI flag and curl parameter syntax are shown as they appear, with placeholders for the tenant ID.)", 'reference': 'To put a tenant into local-only telemetry mode in the control plane, open the tenant config, go to Telemetry, select no-external-telemetry, and apply the change.\nAs a CLI fallback, you can set local-only telemetry mode with: redwoodctl tenant update --id <TENANT> --telemetry-mode local-only.\nYou can verify the telemetry mode by querying http://localhost:9100/telemetry/status?tenant=<TENANT> and checking the returned mode field.\nAfter switching successfully, the reported mode should be local-only.', 'context_precision': 0.99999999995, 'context_recall': 0.75}
