{'user_input': 'In the PRD about adding managed orchestration for multi-model inference pipelines, what are the rollout milestones and target quarters for alpha, beta, and general availability?', 'response': 'Alpha (Q1): API-only pipeline descriptors stored in control plane; planner returns static plans but execution runs as sequential calls (no runtime improvements). Target: 5 internal customers and 2 reference templates.  \nBeta (Q2): Execution fabric accepts envelope requests; add cross-step batching and KV reuse for verified model combinations. Add Console insights.  \nGA (Q3): Add adaptive runtime policies, cost/preference knobs, and enterprise controls for Dedicated/Private. Provide migration tooling.', 'reference': 'Alpha is targeted for Q1.\nAlpha includes API-only pipeline descriptors stored in the control plane.\nAlpha has the planner return static plans with execution as sequential calls and no runtime improvements.\nBeta is targeted for Q2.\nBeta includes an execution fabric that accepts envelope requests.\nBeta adds cross-step batching and KV reuse for verified model combinations.\nBeta adds Console insights.\nGeneral availability is targeted for Q3.\nGA adds adaptive runtime policies and cost/preference knobs.\nGA adds enterprise controls for Dedicated/Private deployments.\nGA includes migration tooling.', 'context_precision': 0.5833333333041666, 'context_recall': 1.0}
