{'user_input': 'We saw quality regressions after enabling an INT8/mixed-precision variant and suspect KV-cache rounding on long-context requests. What request header can we set as a quick mitigation to bypass the KV cache, and in the dynamic quant handoff policy for the interactive-chat route what minimum KV-cache hit-rate and max sequence length are required before routing to a quant variant?', 'response': 'The request header is `X-RW-Cache-Mode: bypass`.\n\nFor the dynamic quant handoff policy for the interactive-chat route, the required minimum KV-cache hit-rate and max sequence length are not found in the provided context.\n\n未找到相关文档。', 'reference': "Setting the request header X-RW-Cache-Mode: bypass bypasses the KV cache.\nFor the interactive-chat dynamic quant handoff policy, routing to a quant variant requires a KV-cache hit-rate of at least 60%.\nFor the interactive-chat dynamic quant handoff policy, routing to a quant variant requires the request sequence length to be at most 2048 tokens.\nThe answer must not use a different cache-bypass header name (e.g., anything other than X-RW-Cache-Mode: bypass).\nThe answer must not claim the interactive-chat route's minimum KV-cache hit-rate is 30% or 0% (those appear for other routes in the routing matrix).\nThe answer must not claim the interactive-chat route's max sequence length for quant routing is 8192 or 1024 (those limits belong to other routes in the routing matrix).\nThe answer must not substitute general quantization rollback/eval thresholds (RSI, fidelity deltas, etc.) in place of the routing requirements requested.", 'context_precision': 0.9999999999, 'context_recall': 0.14285714285714285}
